  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. Here, there are no queries.**\n\nGiven 222 arrays AAA and BBB, both of length NNN, define f(A,B)f(A, B)f(A,B) as follows:\n\n\nChoose 222 intervals [L1,R1][L_1, R_1][L1​,R1​], [L2,R2][L_2, R_2][L2​,R2​] such that:\n\n1≤Li≤Ri≤N1 \\le L_i \\le R_i \\le N1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N\n[L1,R1]∩[L2,R2][L_1, R_1] \\cap [L_2, R_2][L1​,R1​]∩[L2​,R2​] is non-empty, i.e. they share at least one point.\n\n\nThe score of this choice of intervals is defined as ∑i=L1R1Ai+∑i=L2R2Bi\\displaystyle\\sum_{i = L_1}^{R_1} A_i + \\displaystyle\\sum_{i = L_2}^{R_2} B_ii=L1​∑R1​​Ai​+i=L2​∑R2​​Bi​.\nf(L,R)f(L, R)f(L,R) is defined as the maximum possible score under the above constraints.\nLess formally, you have to choose intersecting subarrays from AAA and BBB, and maximize the total sum of the subarrays.\n\nYou are given 222 arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN. Find f(A,B)f(A, B)f(A,B).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains a single integer NNN - the size of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer f(A,B)f(A, B)f(A,B).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "−109≤Ai,Bi≤109-10^9 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^9−109≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
