      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n3\n1 3 -1\n-1 3 1\n2\n2 -1\n-1 2\n3\n-5 -10 -4\n-3 -2 -5\n3\n1 2 3\n3 2 1\n4\n10 -8 -2 6\n-2 3 -5 7",
        "output": "8\n3\n-8\n12\n13",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We can choose [L1,R1]=[1,2][L_1, R_1] = [1, 2][L1​,R1​]=[1,2] and [L2,R2]=[2,3][L_2, R_2] = [2, 3][L2​,R2​]=[2,3], and the score is 1+3+3+1=81 + 3 + 3 + 1 = 81+3+3+1=8.\nTest case 222: We can choose [L1,R1]=[1,2][L_1, R_1] = [1, 2][L1​,R1​]=[1,2] and [L2,R2]=[2,2][L_2, R_2] = [2, 2][L2​,R2​]=[2,2] and the score is 2−1+2=32 - 1 + 2 = 32−1+2=3. We cannot choose [L1,R1]=[1,1][L_1, R_1] = [1, 1][L1​,R1​]=[1,1] and [L2,R2]=[2,2][L_2, R_2] = [2, 2][L2​,R2​]=[2,2] because there is no intersection."
